# Go writes a main package's executable into the working directory, so
# `go build ./evaluation/cmd/<command>` from the repository root leaves the
# binary at the root where `git add -A` will sweep it in. Build into
# generated/bin instead (see the `bin` Makefile target).
#
# TestNoBuildOutputInRepositoryRoot is the actual guard: it rejects any tracked
# root-level binary, including a command added after this list was written.
/generated/bin/
